            <ArticleTitle>Oral medications in the treatment of acute low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>151-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Commonly prescribed drugs for the treatment of low back pain have varying success rates, costs, and complications. This chapter presents current information on acetaminophen, nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory agents, muscle relaxants, opioids, corticosteroids, antidepressants, and colchicine to help the physician in determining a pharmacologic strategy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
